    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our clear offensive engine. Boasting a team-high score of 83.93, **Corbin Carroll** faces Buehler in a matchup that checks every box: a favorable park factor, a +6% platoon advantage, and the premier #2 spot in the order. Similarly, **Max Muncy** provides high-floor production at 71.21 against the lefty Abbott, leveraging a significant +7% platoon boost that cements him as a core play. While **Gabriel Moreno** benefits from a steady +11% SP skill adjustment and a prime #3 hole, his 66.28 score reflects a solid, reliable start rather than the explosive ceiling offered by our top outfield asset.\n\nThe bench decision process was particularly rigorous today, as **Zach McKinstry** finished as the highest-rated reserve with a score of 34.11. While **Zach McKinstry** remains a valuable depth piece for his positional versatility, the matchup against Miller proved too daunting, dragging his efficiency well below our 40.0 threshold. We continue to manage the roster without **James Wood**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Jose Caballero**, who are sidelined due to injury or scheduled rest. Further down the bench, we are monitoring the availability of **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** for potential spot starts as the series progresses.\n\nStrategic caution is warranted regarding **Brice Turang** and **Seiya Suzuki**. **Brice Turang** is currently navigating a difficult matchup against Ashcraft, where an elite catcher pop time effectively nullifies his elite sprint speed potential, capping his score at 51.54. Likewise, **Seiya Suzuki** faces a stiff test in Cease, whose elite arm metrics triggered a -19% SP skill penalty, dragging his projection down to a marginal 48.62. We are also keeping a close eye on **Austin Riley**; while his 58.49 score is respectable, his position in the #8 spot provides minimal run-scoring leverage compared to the top-heavy production we expect from **Travis Bazzana** at the leadoff spot.",
